card.statement:
Let ${\cal G}$ be one of sesquilinear forms <<ref:0.0>>, in which $V$ is a right space over $\mathbb F$, and $U$ is its subspace. Choose a basis $e_1,\dots,e_n$ of\/ $V$ such that

\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
\text{$e_1,\dots,e_m$ is a basis of $U$}
&\text{if
${\cal G}\colon U\times V\to
{\mathbb F}$,}
\\
\text{$e_{m+1},\dots,e_n$ is a
basis of $U$}
&\text{if ${\cal G}\colon (V/U)\times V\to
{\mathbb F}$.}
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

By the matrix of ${\cal
G}$ in the basis $e_1,\dots,e_n$, we mean the block matrix

\begin{equation}
[A|B]=\left.\left[
\begin{matrix}
\alpha_{11}&\dots&\alpha_{1m}\\
\vdots&\ddots&\vdots\\
\alpha_{m1}&\dots&\alpha_{mm}
\end{matrix}
\right|
\begin{matrix}
\alpha_{1,m+1}&\dots&\alpha_{1n}\\
\vdots&&\vdots\\
\alpha_{m,m+1}&\dots&\alpha_{mn}
\end{matrix}
\right],
\end{equation}

in which

\begin{equation*}
\alpha_{ij}=
\begin{cases}
{\cal G} (e_i,e_j) &
\text{if ${\cal
G}\colon U\times V\to {\mathbb
F}$},
\\
{\cal G} (e_i+U,e_j) &
\text{if ${\cal
G}\colon (V/U)\times V\to
{\mathbb F}$}.
\end{cases}
\end{equation*}
